hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"325","Abu Taher informed us, Abu Bakr informed us, Ahmad bin Abdah al-Dhabi informed us, Mughirah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Abdullah, who is Ibn Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah Al-Zarqi, H. Bundar told us, Abu Ahmad told us, Sufyan told us, H. Salam bin Junada, narrated to us by Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah. Waki’ said: On the authority of Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Hakim bin Abbad bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Gabriel called me at the House twice, and he led me in the noon prayer when the sun had set as low as the setting, and he led me in the afternoon prayer when there was shade over everything.” Likewise, he led the sunset prayer with me when the fasting person broke his fast, he led the evening prayer with me when twilight had set, he led the dawn prayer with me when food and drink were forbidden to the fasting person, and he prayed He led me in the afternoon prayer tomorrow when everything was shaded as it was, and he led me in the afternoon prayer when everything was shaded as it was, and he led me in Maghrib prayer when the fasting person broke his fast. He led me in the evening prayer when a third of the night had passed, and he led me in the morning prayer after he had traveled, then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, the time is between these two. “The two times: this is your time and the time of the prophets before you.” “This is the wording of the hadith of Ahmad ibn Abdah, and in the hadith of Waki’: Hakim ibn Hakim Ibn Abbad Ibn Hunaif [Commentary] 325 - Al-Azami said: Its chain of transmission is good."
